  "subtitle": "From your first push-up to the planche — static and dynamic bodyweight strength, built as progressions.",
  "description": "A complete bodyweight strength curriculum, written by an engineer who trains. You start with an honest seven-test assessment and the four pieces of physics that explain every plateau you will ever hit, then work two parallel tracks: **static movements** (support hold, L-sit, handstand, german hang, skin the cat, back lever, front lever, planche) and **dynamic movements** (push-up, dip, pull-up, muscle-up, explosive work). Every progression is explained as a lever problem with the numbers worked out — the diagrams are generated from a segment-mass model, so when a figure says a tuck front lever is 65% of a full one, that was computed rather than guessed. It ends with programming, injury-proofing, and a twelve-week plan you can print and run.",
